    "notes": "Jurassic Finance token sale (jurassic_fi_token_sale) \u2014 a real-world-asset sale: a museum-grade Triceratops skull fractionalised as $TRCH1, live on mainnet. Eight instructions, and SIX of them cannot derive their own root account, because `launch` is seeded on ['launch', launch.admin, launch.launch_id] \u2014 two fields of the account being derived. Orquestra's derive_pda dead-ends here and says so honestly: to compute the account you need what is inside it. Gecko reads admin and launch_id off the chain and derives it, then hands the accounts back to Orquestra's OWN builder. WIDTH IS LOAD-BEARING: params.launch_id is a u64 (le, width 8). Read at u8 it derives a DIFFERENT, perfectly valid address \u2014 correctly formatted, resolvable, and not the sale. No schema check catches that, which is why the width is recovered rather than assumed. In `contribute` the launch_id arrives as an ARGUMENT (params.launch_id), so a caller who knows the sale can supply it; the self-reference only blocks callers who must discover the launch first. Known gap: dust_token_account reads as clean in the IDL but is not buildable from it \u2014 a sibling recipe supplies the missing seed."
